        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.069,
            0.488,
            0.086
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.108,
            0.885,
            0.148
          ],
          "content": "Since π is irrational, there is no ‘best fraction’ for π. If there is any fraction that is close to π, we can find another fraction that is closer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.151,
            0.885,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": "The well-known fraction $\\frac { 2 2 } { 7 }$ is good enough for most practical uses. But it is important to note that π is not equal to $\\frac { 2 2 } { 7 }$ (they are ‘close but not equal’). So we write $\\pi \\approx { \\frac { 2 2 } { 7 } }$ and also $\\pi   \\neq   \\frac { 2 2 } { 7 }$ . In the same way, we can write ${ \\sqrt { 2 } }   \\approx 1 . 4 1 4$ and also ${ \\sqrt { 2 } }   \\neq 1 . 4 1 4$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.27,
            0.801,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": "As noted earlier, a much better approximation for π is ${ \\frac { 3 5 5 } { 1 1 3 } } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.315,
            0.813,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_6_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.633,
            0.231,
            0.652
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Fun Fact"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.661,
            0.738,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": "Here’s a fun way to remember the first few digits of π: How I wish I could recollect $p i .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.719,
            0.883,
            0.77
          ],
          "content": "Count the number of letters in each word (3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2) and you get the digits of π! So, $\\pi \\approx 3 . 1 4 1 5 9 2 .$ …"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.774,
            0.885,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "Since $\\bar { \\pi } \\approx 3 . 1 4$ and also $\\pi \\approx { \\frac { 2 2 } { 7 } }$ , March 14 (written $3 - 1 4$ in North America) is celebrated each year as **Pi Day**, and 22 July (written ‘22-7’ in"
        }
      ]
    }
